on) ships with zero tests; `npm test` passes with no tests. | `devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:443` |\n\n## 5324578247 pullfrog[bot]\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The published getting-started command sequence cannot reach `doctor` on a fresh project because `init` only previews its output without writing the manifest. The optional Cloudflare deployment path also needs a search URL within the docs route scope before it is enabled.\n\n**Reviewed changes** The new DevFn DocsFn consumer site, generated content artifacts, SvelteKit routing, and workspace integration were reviewed.\n\n- **Consumer documentation:** Adds introductory, operational, security, migration, configuration, and package-reference pages with navigation and generated LLM indexes.\n- **Site runtime:** Bundles source Markdown into a DocsFn manifest and search index, serves compiled docs pages and a search artifact, and configures optional Cloudflare builds.\n- **Workspace integration:** Registers `@devfn/docs` and its dependencies in the npm lockfile.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against b84bae1b;\nif commits have landed on codex/docs-devfn-20260926 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: Review (initial)\n- Files reviewed: 49\n- Commits reviewed: 1\n- Base: dev (7c6ec512)\n- Head: codex/docs-devfn-20260926 (b84bae1b)\n- Reviewed commits:\n  - b84bae1b — docs(devfn): add DocsFn consumer site\n- Prior pullfrog review: none\n-->\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/212?action=fix&review_id=5