{"type":"message","id":"e73e64c5","parentId":"03e73b1e","timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:25:19.742Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_680HouBohzxhokJVwkRPI4A7|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3dd7f738c87d0b394cf4d3fc672fb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 5843033170 qodo-code-review[bot]\n<!-- qodo:billing-blocked -->\n\n**ⓘ Qodo reviews are paused because the subscription is no longer active.** Ask your workspace admin to reactivate the subscription to resume reviews. [Manage billing](https://app.qodo.ai/account/billing/manage-subscription?traffic_source=pr_comment)\n\n## 5843033285 mira-rhombus[bot]\n<!-- mira-walkthrough -->\n## Mira PR Walkthrough\n\nThis PR wires the DevFn documentation site into the shared DocsFn infrastructure and refactors all three docs sites (DevFn, AuthFn, FileFn) to consume a canonical shared runtime under `scripts/docs-site`. A new shared `page.ts` module collapses ~110 lines of duplicated route-loader logic per site, while `llms.mjs` gains shared helpers for generating `llms.txt` artifacts. CI and Cloudflare deployment workflows are updated to build and route the DevFn docs alongside existing sites.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n  runtime[\"docs-site/page.ts\"]\n  llms[\"docs-site/llms.mjs\"]\n  devfn[\"devfn +page.server.ts\"]\n  authfn[\"authfn +page.server.ts\"]\n  filefn[\"filefn +page.server.ts\"]\n  genllms[\"generate-llms.mjs scripts\"]\n  devfn --> runtime\n  authfn --> runtime\n  filefn --> runtime\n  genllms --> llms\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Confidence: 4/5</b> &nbsp; ◉◉◉◉○ &nbsp; Safe with minor fixes</summary>\n\n- The change is predominantly mechanical deduplication validated by runtime tests; the only residual risk is subtle behavioral drift in the slimmed route loaders across the three sites.\n\n</details>\n\n> **⚠️ Potential overlap with other open PRs** — these may be stepping on this one:\n>\n> - [#225](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/225) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Introduces the same shared scripts/docs-site runtime and edits the same authfn/filefn docs scaffolding as #212, duplicating that infrastructure and guaranteeing a collision. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#224](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/224) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Duplicates #212's shared scripts/docs-site runtime introduction and edits the same authfn/filefn docs files, so the redundant scaffolding will conflict. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#222](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/222) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Adds the same scripts/docs-site shared runtime and touches the same authfn/filefn docs wiring as #212, making the duplicated infrastructure collide on merge. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#220](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/220) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Introduces the same shared scripts/docs-site runtime (including runtime.test.ts) and the same authfn/filefn docs edits as #212, so both the duplication and file collisions apply. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +20 more\n> - [#221](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/221) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Duplicates the shared scripts/docs-site runtime and authfn/filefn docs scaffolding from #212, so merging both will collide on the redundant files. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#219](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/219) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Introduces the same scripts/docs-site shared runtime and edits the same authfn/filefn docs files as #212, duplicating infrastructure that will conflict. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +18 more\n> - [#218](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/218) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Adds the same shared scripts/docs-site runtime and touches the same authfn/filefn docs scaffolding as #212, so the duplicated work will collide. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +18 more\n> - [#217](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/217) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Introduces the same scripts/docs-site runtime and the same authfn/filefn docs wiring as #212, duplicating infrastructure that will conflict on merge. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +19 more\n> - [#216](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/216) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Adds the same shared scripts/docs-site runtime and edits the same authfn/filefn docs scaffolding as #212, duplicating infrastructure that will collide. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#213](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/213) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Introduces the same scripts/docs-site shared runtime and the same authfn/filefn docs edits as #212, so the redundant scaffolding will conflict. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#210](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/210) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Duplicates #212's shared scripts/docs-site runtime and authfn/filefn docs wiring edits, guaranteeing both redundant work and merge collisions. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` +21 more\n> - [#209](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/209) (duplicate effort + merge-conflict risk) — Introduces the same shared scripts/docs-site runtime (including runtime.test.ts) and the same authfn/filefn docs edits as #212, duplicating infrastructure that will collide. Shared: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `authfn/docs/package.json` +20 more\n> - [#207](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/207) (merge-conflict risk) — Despite a different content goal, it edits the same scripts/docs-site runtime files and authfn/filefn docs wiring as #212, risking a collision. Shared: `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml`, `authfn/docs/package.json`, `authfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs` +15 more\n\n\n> **Blast Radius** — 1 dependent repository, 2 total references\n>\n> `21nCo/omr` — 2 references\n\n\n*22 files reviewed · 2 unresolved threads*\n\n---\n> Comment `@mira-rhombus help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.\n\n## 5843033480 kody-ai[bot]\n## Code Review Could Not Complete ⚠️\n\nThe review failed before suggestions could be generated.\n\n**Reason:** The configured API key (open_router) is out of credits or has hit its billing limit. Top up the account or adjust the plan.\n\nopen_router · z-ai/glm-5.3 · HTTP 402 · generalist\n\nProvider