rst-colon identities own source filenames; actual filename/index semantics determine relative links, never descendant-route heuristics or invented DocPage fields. Full content/search/manifests and body/frontmatter stay server-owned; only permitted route/layout DTO fields cross browser data. Consumer-owned public ESM/subpath exports, real Kit/parser/search peers and roots resolve under supported Node policy; no guessed CJS directory/index.js, universal externalization, root fallback or borrowed application dependencies. Provider listEntries/loadEntry remain Promise/rejection methods despite Sonar async-without-await reports. Six raw-text extensions remain native texts while binary static files pass through. LLM producers distinguish public documentation origin from assets/CDN origin, preserving212 canonicalUrl option/returned value and source fallback when no assigned public origin exists. Current normal dynamic titles must remain single; errors also own their title. DevFn native search/TopBar/mobile drawer, correct lifecycle state-directory/secret/migration/init warnings, sidebar fallback and registry/workflow product wiring must be preserved.\n\n## 2. Faithful old evidence\nFresh audit-only exact frozen runtime/page executed against real published SDK0.0.5: flat.md plus flat/child.md causes the actual compiled sibling anchor to become `/docs/flat/sibling.md`, rather than SDK route `/docs/sibling`; `frozen-published-boundary.log` and SSD `frozen212-focused-sdk-boundary/frozen212-published-provider-boundary.json`. No invented DocPage fields. Existing211 AuthFn installed public SDK/compiler were probe tooling only; this is not frozen212 native Vite, physical consumer or lock-install proof.\n\nComplete current source shows AuthFn page forwards full parent source, shared factory exists and gets full bodies, AuthFn/FileFn eager all-static raw globs and DevFn narrower3-extension glob, guessed conditional exports in plugin, missing shared Kit/parser consumer handling, and source-by-descendant index heuristic. Frozen canonical regex contains super-linear trailing-slash scan and nested template; unused AuthFn source import is genuinely unused. Current test config parses JSON into implicit-any and may crash on nonstring name before its invocation hint. Concrete failure cases and further old native/serialized negatives must be reproduced before accepting their coordinated repair, not inferred from older different page/plugin/LLM bytes. `related-old-source-equivalence.json` proves only specified exact matches; page/plugin/LLM differ from old210, so do not automatically transfer those negatives.\n\nFrozen JavaScript once-retrieved log reproduces SecFn audit missing configurableIsolation and transaction arity; current source APIs are correct, installed prerequisite DB owner is stale. Frozen Sonar6 annotations: three quality concerns (canonical regex/template and unused import), three incorrect-context concerns (two required provider async interfaces and template title already supplied dynamically). No hosted pass inferred. Security threads are stale for DevFn's own locked Vite6.4.3/Svelte5.55.7, not global root-version clearance. Current title template has no static title, and current LLM wrapper explicitly carries canonicalUrl override and return—preserve these positives.\n\n## 3. Coordinated ownership/failure plan\nCompose complete original75 scope over exact reviewed42a prerequisites using one existing SSD candidate. Restore nonapplicable211 source to42a; no blind full210 feature transfer or CliFn/BotFn expansion. Reuse only explicitly traced reviewed210 shared/public-consumer repairs applicable to DevFn/AuthFn/FileFn; inspect differences and preserve unique212 API fallback, canonicalUrl option/return, package pins/test example/Node policy, actual native search/mobile/observer cleanup and reduced-motion positives. Independent source absences come from exact Git tree membership, not potentially-successful pathspec `git show`. Explicit Git120000 link text and executable modes are part of guards.\n\nArchive candidate source preimages/absences and previous211 installed metadata/public SDK history before reuse; verify all canonical preimages and outside-plan bytes/modes. Focused exact owner lock maps only, preserve newest prerequisites; no whole lock normalization, force/legacy peers, copied standalone/root locks or installation surgery. Adapt only consumer-specific verifiers. Existing3 standalone contexts remain untouched unless separately owner-admitted and genuinely necessary; no fourth or retained full root. SSD UUID/cache/temp/reserve revalidated before necessary ordinary installation.\n\n## 4. Independent acceptance\nFresh distinguishing old SDK/provider/serialization and resolver/text/title/LLM/input cases; current compiled anchor equals real SDK manifest route. Actual public exported package resolution and physical dependency closures inside admitted roots, ordinary root npm-ci with scripts and unchanged lock. Consumer tests/real types, fresh prerequisite generator/build order, all three affected native builds and HTTP/serialized payloads/source/Unicode/API/sidebar/normal-error-title/search/LLM/native binary passthrough; lifecycle/browser proof where affected, not a thin-fixture substitute. Actual offline Cloudflare artifacts only, never live upload/domain/routes/secrets. Source fallback has exact canonical ID/source path, public/assets origins independently tested. Controlled inputs absent before final builds/source capture. Original75 scope, current base dependencies/workflows/locks/protected paths, full canonical byte/mode/index/ancestry guard and final reviewed diff required before publication. Frozen31-thread/check dispositions plus new supplementary defects/gaps retained. One ordinary commit/push at most, Entire enabled, one immediate receipt, stop; no merge without applicable-green exact hosted assessment, no post-push refetch/poll/automatic stopped-PR revisit.\n\nCurrent admission: read-only assessment/audit probes and planning only. No candidate application/native-install/promotion/publication authority has passed its specific guards yet. Excluded live/backend/SQL skips/global security/native platform and any failed baseline type gates remain qualified, not accepted risk.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":918,"output":1928,"cacheRead":179072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":516,"totalTokens":181918,"cost":{"input":0.001836,"output":0.019280000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0179072,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03902320000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791221498941,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3defb8a4c87d09c3a2ff11b2ac040","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
