ven byte-equal current candidate/default base. Admit collision-free child renames into that existing namespace; preserve this file and old empty dirs, never delete/replace an unknown target. This is not further historical cleanup or the consumed two-tree relocation. Preserve all installations/locks/build outputs/hardlinked binaries and uncertain artifacts. Remove only archive-verified obsolete former CliFn application-source inputs proved absent from actual new DevFn source; no dependency surgery or unverified cleanup. Current AuthFn/FileFn declarations are expected exact current candidate and may retain installed context/own lock; copying current source/shared helpers is not root application dependency borrowing.\n 6 \n 7 Only DevFn's changed declaration requires a fresh ordinary npm11 standalone install into its own existing context/lock, with scripts enabled, SSD-routed cache/temp/gyp/XDG/UUID/writability/same-filesystem/fresh reserve. No root or sibling lock copied. Revalidate actual owners/closures/public exports and run actual independent tests/types/build/dev/HTTP/LLM cases in all3 contexts. Never count historical210 pass as current212 acceptance. Current source/archives/install/root native receipts remain distinct; publication/promotion and hosted/live gates remain closed. No unrelated worktree, .conduct/.entire/traineddata, infrastructure/registry/reviewer changes.","patch":"--- /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-212/standalone-reuse-admission.md\n+++ /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-212/standalone-reuse-admission.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n # Necessary independent consumer-owner verification — PR212\n \n Actual212 owns a new DevFn DocsFn consumer and changes the shared conditional/Kit/parser/peer/LLM ownership boundary used by AuthFn/FileFn. Root installation/build/type/tests/physical closure is insufficient proof that this contract works without parent application dependencies. Therefore use only the existing3 physical standalone contexts, not a fourth consumer or another full root.\n \n-Admit guarded source/lock/installed metadata/public SDK archive, verified bytes/modes/relative links before changes, and same-filesystem namespace reuse of the existing CliFn/docs context as DevFn/docs. This is not further historical cleanup or the consumed two-tree relocation. Preserve all installations/locks/build outputs/hardlinked binaries and uncertain artifacts. Remove only archive-verified obsolete former CliFn application-source inputs proved absent from actual new DevFn source; no dependency surgery or unverified cleanup. Current AuthFn/FileFn declarations are expected exact current candidate and may retain installed context/own lock; copying current source/shared helpers is not root application dependency borrowing.\n+Admit guarded source/lock/installed metadata/public SDK archive, verified bytes/modes/relative links before changes, and same-filesystem namespace reuse of the existing CliFn/docs context as DevFn/docs. Initial no-target-dir guard failed before archives/writes: an existing DevFn/docs/configuration.md is the sole target child, proven byte-equal current candidate/default base. Admit collision-free child renames into that existing namespace; preserve this file and old empty dirs, never delete/replace an unknown target. This is not further historical cleanup or the consumed two-tree relocation. Preserve all installations/locks/build outputs/hardlinked binaries and uncertain artifacts. Remove only archive-verified obsolete former CliFn application-source inputs proved absent from actual new DevFn source; no dependency surgery or unverified cleanup. Current AuthFn/FileFn declarations are expected exact current candidate and may retain installed context/own lock; copying current source/shared helpers is not root application dependency borrowing.\n \n Only DevFn's changed declaration requires a fresh ordinary npm11 standalone install into its own existing context/lock, with scripts enabled, SSD-routed cache/temp/gyp/XDG/UUID/writability/same-filesystem/fresh reserve. No root or sibling lock copied. Revalidate actual owners/closures/public exports and run actual independent tests/types/build/dev/HTTP/LLM cases in all3 contexts. Never count historical210 pass as current212 acceptance. Current source/archives/install/root native receipts remain distinct; publication/promotion and hosted/live gates remain closed. No unrelated worktree, .conduct/.entire/traineddata, infrastructure/registry/reviewer changes.\n","firstChangedLine":5},"isError":false,"timestamp":1791223815900}}
