{"type":"message","id":"6989a769","parentId":"adfbae86","timestamp":"2026-10-05T18:23:43.162Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_qNZaJcqEy3DxcSxyJrKHvrUb|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3eb2eed7887d0a583a45d326e7b34","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import type { DocHeading, DocsTopNavItem, Sidebar, Version } from \"@docsfn/core/browser\";\n  import DocsSidebar from \"./DocsSidebar.svelte\";\n  import DocsToc from \"./DocsToc.svelte\";\n\n  export interface DocsPageLink {\n    title: string;\n    path: string;\n  }\n\n  export interface DocsPageBreadcrumbItem {\n    label: string;\n    href: string;\n  }\n\n  export interface DocsPagePagination {\n    prev?: DocsPageLink;\n    next?: DocsPageLink;\n  }\n\n  export interface DocsPageSurface {\n    route: string;\n    title?: string;\n    description?: string;\n    canonicalPath?: string;\n    canonicalUrl?: string;\n    editLink?: string;\n    pageActions?: Array<Record<string, unknown>>;\n    sidebar?: Sidebar;\n    sidebarId?: string;\n    headings?: DocHeading[];\n    breadcrumbs?: DocsPageBreadcrumbItem[];\n    pagination?: DocsPagePagination;\n    topNav?: DocsTopNavItem[];\n    versions?: Version[];\n    currentVersion?: string;\n    versionLinks?: Record<string, string>;\n  }\n\n  export let surface: DocsPageSurface | undefined = undefined;\n  export let sidebar: Sidebar | undefined = undefined;\n  export let headings: DocHeading[] | undefined = undefined;\n  export let activePath: string | undefined = undefined;\n\n  $: resolvedSidebar = sidebar ?? surface?.sidebar;\n  $: resolvedHeadings = headings ?? surface?.headings ?? [];\n  $: resolvedActivePath = activePath ?? surface?.route;\n\n  let sidebarOpen = false;\n</script>\n\n<div class=\"docsfn-layout\">\n  {#if $$slots.topbar}\n    <header class=\"docsfn-topbar\">\n      <slot name=\"topbar\" />\n    </header>\n  {/if}\n\n  {#if resolvedSidebar}\n    <div class=\"docsfn-mobile-toolbar\">\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        class=\"docsfn-mobile-menu-btn\"\n        aria-expanded={sidebarOpen}\n        aria-controls=\"docsfn-sidebar-panel\"\n        on:click={() => (sidebarOpen = !sidebarOpen)}\n      >\n        Menu\n      </button>\n    </div>\n\n    {#if sidebarOpen}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        class=\"docsfn-mobile-backdrop\"\n        aria-label=\"Close menu\"\n        on:click={() => (sidebarOpen = false)}\n      ></button>\n    {/if}\n  {/if}\n\n  <div class=\"docsfn-container\">\n    {#if resolvedSidebar}\n      <aside\n        id=\"docsfn-sidebar-panel\"\n        class=\"docsfn-sidebar-col\"\n        class:docsfn-sidebar-col--open={sidebarOpen}\n      >\n        <DocsSidebar surface={surface} sidebar={resolvedSidebar} activePath={resolvedActivePath} />\n      </aside>\n    {/if}\n\n    <main class=\"docsfn-main\">\n      <slot />\n    </main>\n\n    {#if resolvedHeadings.length > 0}\n      <aside class=\"docsfn-toc-col\">\n        <DocsToc surface={surface} headings={resolvedHeadings} />\n      </aside>\n    {/if}\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<style>\n  .docsfn-mobile-toolbar {\n    display: block;\n    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docsfn-color-border, #e2e8f0);\n    background: var(--docsfn-color-surface, #fff);\n  }\n\n  @media (min-width: 1024px) {\n    /* Remove from layout flow entirely (avoids stray gap above .docsfn-container). */\n    .docsfn-mobile-toolbar {\n      display: none !important;\n      height: 0;\n      min-height: 0;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      border: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n  }\n\n  .docsfn-mobile-menu-btn {\n    font: inherit;\n    font-size: 0.875rem;\n    padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;\n    border-radius: 0.375rem;\n    border: 1px solid var(--docsfn-color-border, #e2e8f0);\n    background: var(--docsfn-color-surface, #fff);\n    cursor: pointer;\n  }\n\n  .docsfn-mobile-backdrop {\n    position: fixed;\n    inset: 0;\n    z-index: 30;\n    border: none;\n\n[27 more lines in file. Use offset=141 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791224623162}}
{"type":"message","id":"9cb0e96f","parentId":"6989a769","timestamp":"2026-10-05T18:23:43.162Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_hrz4Uk5kX4detqudtOck55Gt|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3eb2eed9087d099dda380d9e45a55","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createDocsSearchRuntime, type DocsSearchRuntimeResultItem } from \"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\";\n\n  let dialog: HTMLDialogElement;\n  let input: HTMLInputElement;\n  let query = $state(\"\");\n  let results = $state<DocsSearchRuntimeResultItem[]>([]);\n  let pending = $state(false);\n  let failure = $state(\"\");\n  let requestId = 0;\n  const runtime = createDocsSearchRuntime({\n    loadArtifact: async () => {\n      const response = await fetch(\"/docs/search.json\");\n      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(\"Could not load documentation search.\");\n      return response.json();\n    },\n  });\n\n  function openSearch() {\n    if (!dialog.open) dialog.showModal();\n    input.focus();\n  }\n\n  function shortcut(event: KeyboardEvent) {\n    if ((event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey) && event.key.toLowerCase() === \"k\") {\n      event.preventDefault();\n      openSearch();\n    }\n  }\n\n  async function search() {\n    const current = ++requestId;\n    failure = \"\";\n    results = [];\n    pending = Boolean(query.trim());\n    if (!pending) return;\n    try {\n      const found = await runtime.query({ query, scope: \"all\", limit: 10 });\n      if (current === requestId) results = found;\n    } catch {\n      if (current === requestId) failure = \"Search is unavailable. Please try again.\";\n    } finally {\n      if (current === requestId) pending = false;\n    }\n  }\n</script>\n\n<svelte:window onkeydown={shortcut} />\n<button class=\"docsfn-search-trigger\" type=\"button\" onclick={openSearch} aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">\n  Search <span aria-hidden=\"true\">⌘/Ctrl K</span>\n</button>\n<dialog bind:this={dialog} aria-labelledby=\"docs-search-title\">\n  <div class=\"search-heading\">\n    <h2 id=\"docs-search-title\">Search documentation</h2>\n    <button type=\"button\" onclick={() => dialog.close()} aria-label=\"Close search\">Close</button>\n  </div>\n  <label for=\"docs-search-query\">Search terms</label>\n  <input id=\"docs-search-query\" bind:this={input} value={query} oninput={(event) => { query = event.currentTarget.value; void search(); }} type=\"search\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"Search documentation…\" />\n  <p role=\"status\">{failure ? \"\" : pending ? \"Searching…\" : query.trim() ? `${results.length} results` : \"Enter a term to search.\"}</p>\n  {#if failure}<p role=\"alert\">{failure}</p>{/if}\n  <ul>\n    {#each results as result (`${result.id}:${result.path}`)}\n      <li><a href={result.path} onclick={() => dialog.close()}>{result.title}</a></li>\n    {/each}\n  </ul>\n</dialog>\n\n<style>\n  button { cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid var(--docsfn-color-border); border-radius: .375rem; padding: .45rem .65rem; color: var(--docsfn-color-fg); background: var(--docsfn-color-surface); }\n  .docsfn-search-trigger { display: flex; gap: .75rem; align-items: center; }\n  .docsfn-search-trigger span { font-size: .7rem; color: var(--docsfn-color-muted); }\n  dialog { box-sizing: border-box; width: min(38rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)); max-height: 80vh; padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--docsfn-color-border); border-radius: .75rem; background: var(--docsfn-color-surface); color: var(--docsfn-color-fg); }\n  dialog::backdrop { background: rgb(15 23 42 / .45); }\n  .search-heading { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }\n  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0; }\n  label { display: block; margin-bottom: .35rem; }\n  input { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; padding: .65rem; border: 1px solid var(--docsfn-color-border); border-radius: .375rem; color: inherit; background: var(--docsfn-color-bg); }\n  p { font-size: .875rem; }\n  ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }\n  a { display: block; padding: .65rem; color: var(--docsfn-color-primary); border-radius: .25rem; }\n  a:hover, a:focus-visible { background: var(--docsfn-color-accent-soft); }\n  @media (max-width: 600px) { .docsfn-search-trigger span { display: none; } }\n</style>\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791224623162}}
{"type":"message","id":"f93723af","parentId":"9cb0e96f","timestamp":"2026-10-05T18:23:43.162Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Z8pdTflIRUvTEGnefvfhLghq|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3eb2eed9c87d099466dc5d80f2c71","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# PR212 current frozen round — pre-mutation architecture reset\n\nFrozen0680df1ee45cd4797f574bc99489d2dc1d1532ca; one collection31threads/8primary/75paths. Preparation default42a differs PR/check base7c6; retain both. Hosted1.4.0 revision6 exact digest; prior212 ledger retained. Old212 title/test-hint repairs remain correct, not regressions. Broader shared subsystem has two evidenced failed related206/207 rounds and qualified/incomplete sibling histories; counter is not reset by this new product. Emit ARCHITECTURE_RESET_REQUIRED:docs.page-provider-path-and-payload and docs.consumer-conditional-runtime-ownership. Mode architecture_reset; publication remains closed until complete executing-boundary/native assessment.\n\n## 1. Shared invariant\nPublished DocsFn0.0.5 canonical first-colon identities own source filenames; actual filename/index semantics determine relative links, never descendant-route heuristics or invented DocPage fields. Full content/search/manifests and body/frontmatter stay server-owned; only permitted route/layout DTO fields cross browser data. Consumer-owned public ESM/subpath exports, real Kit/parser/search peers and roots resolve under supported Node policy; no guessed CJS directory/index.js, universal externalization, root fallback or borrowed application dependencies. Provider listEntries/loadEntry remain Promise/rejection methods despite Sonar async-without-await reports. Six raw-text extensions remain native texts while binary static files pass through. LLM producers distinguish public documentation origin from assets/CDN origin, preserving212 canonicalUrl option/returned value and source fallback when no assigned public origin exists. Current normal dynamic titles must remain single; errors also own their title. DevFn native search/TopBar/mobile drawer, correct lifecycle state-directory/secret/migration/init warnings, sidebar fallback and registry/workflow product wiring must be preserved.\n\n## 2. Faithful old evidence\nFresh audit-only exact frozen runtime/page executed against real published SDK0.0.5: flat.md plus flat/child.md causes the actual compiled sibling anchor to become `/docs/flat/sibling.md`, rather than SDK route `/docs/sibling`; `frozen-published-boundary.log` and SSD `frozen212-focused-sdk-boundary/frozen212-published-provider-boundary.json`. No invented DocPage fields. Existing211 AuthFn installed public SDK/compiler were probe tooling only; this is not frozen212 native Vite, physical consumer or lock-install proof.\n\nComplete current source shows AuthFn page forwards full parent source, shared factory exists and gets full bodies, AuthFn/FileFn eager all-static raw globs and DevFn narrower3-extension glob, guessed conditional exports in plugin, missing shared Kit/parser consumer handling, and source-by-descendant index heuristic. Frozen canonical regex contains super-linear trailing-slash scan and nested template; unused AuthFn source import is genuinely unused. Current test config parses JSON into implicit-any and may crash on nonstring name before its invocation hint. Concrete failure cases and further old native/serialized negatives must be reproduced before accepting their coordinated repair, not inferred from older different page/plugin/LLM bytes. `related-old-source-equivalence.json` proves only specified exact matches; page/plugin/LLM differ from old210, so do not automatically transfer those negatives.\n\nFrozen JavaScript once-retrieved log reproduces SecFn audit missing configurableIsolation and transaction arity; current source APIs are correct, installed prerequisite DB owner is stale. Frozen Sonar6 annotations: three quality concerns (canonical regex/template and unused import), three incorrect-context concerns (two required provider async interfaces and template title already supplied dynamically). No hosted pass inferred. Security threads are stale for DevFn's own locked Vite6.4.3/Svelte5.55.7, not global root-version clearance. Current title template has no static title, and current LLM wrapper explicitly carries canonicalUrl override and return—preserve these positives.\n\n## 3. Coordinated ownership/failure plan\nCompose complete original75 scope over exact reviewed42a prerequisites using one existing SSD candidate. Restore nonapplicable211 source to42a; no blind full210 feature transfer or CliFn/BotFn expansion. Reuse only explicitly traced reviewed210 shared/public-consumer repairs applicable to DevFn/AuthFn/FileFn; inspect differences and preserve unique212 API fallback, canonicalUrl option/return, package pins/test example/Node policy, actual native search/mobile/observer cleanup and reduced-motion positives. Independent source absences come from exact Git tree membership, not potentially-successful pathspec `git show`. Explicit Git120000 link text and executable modes are part of guards.\n\nArchive candidate source preimages/absences and previous211 installed metadata/public SDK history before reuse; verify all canonical preimages and outside-plan bytes/modes. Focused exact owner lock maps only, preserve newest prerequisites; no whole lock normalization, force/legacy peers, copied standalone/root locks or installation surgery. Adapt only consumer-specific verifiers. Existing3 standalone contexts remain untouched unless separately owner-admitted and genuinely necessary; no fourth or retained full root. SSD UUID/cache/temp/reserve revalidated before necessary ordinary installation.\n\n## 4. Independent acceptance\nFresh distinguishing old SDK/provider/serialization and resolver/text/title/LLM/input cases; current compiled anchor equals real SDK manifest route. Actual public exported package resolution and physical dependency closures inside admitted roots, ordinary root npm-ci with scripts and unchanged lock. Consumer tests/real types, fresh prerequisite generator/build order, all three affected native builds and HTTP/serialized payloads/source/Unicode/API/sidebar/normal-error-title/search/LLM/native binary passthrough; lifecycle/browser proof where affected, not a thin-fixture substitute. Actual offline Cloudflare artifacts only, never live upload/domain/routes/secrets. Source fallback has exact canonical ID/source path, public/assets origins independently tested. Controlled inputs absent before final builds/source capture. Original75 scope, current base dependencies/workflows/locks/protected paths, full canonical byte/mode/index/ancestry guard and final reviewed diff required before publication. Frozen31-thread/check dispositions plus new supplementary defects/gaps retained. One ordinary commit/push at most, Entire enabled, one immediate receipt, stop; no merge without applicable-green exact hosted assessment, no post-push refetch/poll/automatic stopped-PR revisit.\n\nCurrent admission: read-only assessment/audit probes and planning only. No candidate application/native-install/promotion/publication authority has passed its specific guards yet. Excluded live/backend/SQL skips/global security/native platform and any failed baseline type gates remain qualified, not accepted risk.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791224623162}}
